{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Eraka","html":"<article id='thag1.93'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.93 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.93 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dasamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Ten </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Erakattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Eraka </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dukkhā kāmā eraka, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sensual pleasures are suffering, Eraka! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na sukhā kāmā eraka; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sensual pleasures aren’t happiness, Eraka! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo kāme kāmayati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who enjoys sensual pleasures </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dukkhaṁ so kāmayati eraka; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>enjoys suffering, Eraka! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo kāme na kāmayati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who doesn’t enjoy sensual pleasures </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dukkhaṁ so na kāmayati erakā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>doesn’t enjoy suffering, Eraka! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Erako thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
